          <h2 class="text-2xl font-black text-white mb-4">The Bottom Line</h2>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            The best ultrasonic humidifier for most homes is the Levoit LV600S: a 6-liter top-fill tank, warm and cool mist, and a sensor that holds your target humidity. The Dreo HM713S does nearly the same job for less, the OasisMist 1000S halves your refills, and the Boneco U350 is the one to buy if hard water is your main worry.
          </p>
          <p class="text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-4">
            Whichever you choose, the water and the cleaning matter more than the model. Use distilled or low-mineral water if yours is hard, empty the tank daily, clean it every third day, and keep a hygrometer in the room so you aim for 30 to 50 percent. Do that, and an ultrasonic humidifier is the quietest, cheapest way to fix dry winter air.
